================================================================================
BOOTSTRAP UNCERTAINTY — 1000 resamples of the 5216 test patients, 95% percentile intervals (Gap 3)
================================================================================
Only test patients are resampled; the training-set censoring reference is held fixed (see pkgs/data_analysis/bootstrap_ci.py for why).
C-index resamples retain full follow-up; IBS/AUC alone use the IPCW-capped outcomes. Numerically constant rankings are withheld from points, intervals and paired differences.
Bootstrap AUC uses a 25-point grid over 0-729d rather than the per-day grid of the point estimate — see bootstrap_ci.py.

C-index — estimate [95% CI]:
  DeepSurv             0.5333 [0.5234, 0.5416]  (n=1000)

Integrated Brier — estimate [95% CI]:
  DeepSurv             0.2308 [0.2282, 0.2337]  (n=1000)  (Brier source: fitted-conversion)

Mean time-dependent AUC — estimate [95% CI]:
  DeepSurv             0.5559 [0.5403, 0.5683]  (n=1000)

Paired differences vs. best model by C-index (DeepSurv), same resamples (positive = the listed model is higher):
  C-index and AUC: higher is better. Integrated Brier: LOWER is better, so a negative difference favours the listed model.
  * interval excludes 0. These are 95% percentile intervals on paired differences, not multiplicity-controlled tests across the model set.

